{"v":3,"src":"MOV     AH, 5Bh          ; DOS: create TEST.TXT, which must be new\nXOR     CX, CX\nMOV     DX, OFFSET FNAME\nINT     21h\nCALL    CHECK\nMOV     BX, AX\nMOV     AH, 3Eh          ; close it\nINT     21h\nMOV     DX, OFFSET M1\nMOV     AH, 09h          ; DOS: print the string at DS:DX\nINT     21h\nMOV     DX, OFFSET M2\nMOV     AH, 09h          ; DOS: print the string at DS:DX\nINT     21h\nMOV     AH, 5Bh          ; again: now the file exists\nXOR     CX, CX\nMOV     DX, OFFSET FNAME\nINT     21h\nCALL    REPORT           ; CF = 1, AX = 50h\nMOV     AH, 41h          ; delete TEST.TXT\nMOV     DX, OFFSET FNAME\nINT     21h\n\nFNAME   DB      \"TEST.TXT\", 0\nM1      DB      \"first 5Bh: created\", 13, 10, \"$\"\nM2      DB      \"second 5Bh: $\"\nCRLF    DB      13, 10, \"$\"\nCHECK   PROC    NEAR     ; CF = 1: print the error code in AL and exit\nJNC     CHECK1\nPUSH    AX\nMOV     DX, OFFSET FAILMSG\nMOV     AH, 09h\nINT     21h\nPOP     AX\nCALL    PHEXB\nMOV     AX, 4C01h        ; exit with code 1\nINT     21h\nCHECK1:\nRET\nCHECK   ENDP\nFAILMSG DB      \"failed: error $\"\nREPORT  PROC    NEAR     ; CF = 0: \"ok\"; CF = 1: \"error\" and AL\nJC      REPORT1\nMOV     DX, OFFSET OKMSG\nMOV     AH, 09h\nINT     21h\nRET\nREPORT1:\nPUSH    AX\nMOV     DX, OFFSET ERRMSG\nMOV     AH, 09h\nINT     21h\nPOP     AX\nCALL    PHEXB            ; the error code\nMOV     DX, OFFSET CRLF\nMOV     AH, 09h\nINT     21h\nRET\nREPORT  ENDP\nOKMSG   DB      \"ok\", 13, 10, \"$\"\nERRMSG  DB      \"error $\"\nPHEXB   PROC    NEAR     ; print AL as two hex digits\nPUSH    CX\nPUSH    DX\nMOV     DH, AL           ; keep the byte\nMOV     CL, 4\nSHR     AL, CL           ; the high digit first\nMOV     CX, 2\nPHEXB1:\nAND     AL, 0Fh\nADD     AL, \"0\"\nCMP     AL, \"9\"\nJBE     PHEXB2\nADD     AL, 7            ; 10..15 -> \"A\"..\"F\"\nPHEXB2:\nMOV     DL, AL\nMOV     AH, 02h          ; DOS: print DL\nINT     21h\nMOV     AL, DH           ; then the low digit\nLOOP    P